# Benchmarks

Correctness first, then **measure on the same PR**. Phase 2 is for speeding up. Do not wait until Phase 2 to time or count allocations.

- Time: [criterion](https://docs.rs/criterion). Entry `benches/exact.rs`. Command `just bench`.
- Allocations: `tests/alloc.rs` runs in `just test`. Count after Workspace setup. Ratchet: the allowed count must stay or fall, never rise without an Issue.
- Fixed problem: RNG seed `0`, `d = 8`, RBF + `GaussianLikelihood`, hypers fixed. Sizes `n = 256` (required from P1A-18), then `512` / `1024` when they finish in seconds. P2-7 adds ARD RBF groups on that same problem (`mll_and_grad_ard` / `fit_lbfgs_ard`). Compare Always vs Never; do not compare those groups to isotropic `phase-1b`.
- Split benches. Never mix "one MLL+grad" with "full L-BFGS fit".
- `just bench` is local. Default CI does not run criterion (noisy). Alloc tests stay in `just test`.
- PR that touches a hot path (`kernel/`, `workspace`, `gpr`, `objective`, `online`): paste criterion vs previous named baseline in Verification, or write why it cannot change speed.
- Do not add SIMD, Rayon, mixed precision, or cache "for speed" unless a bench on this problem shows that path is the bottleneck. Isotropic RBF / distance SIMD is already in (`src/kernel/simd.rs`). ARD `(Δx_d)²` fill and RBF ARD `apply`/`grad` SIMD are in with the P2-7 cache. Judge more SIMD on `kernel_rbf` / `predict` / `FIXED` / ARD kernel paths, not only on `mll_and_grad`.
- Named baselines: `phase-1a`, `phase-1b`, `phase-2`. Save with criterion; log the machine and the numbers in `.dev/bench-log.md`. After P2-9, compare new work to `phase-2` (isotropic vs `phase-1b` is historical; ARD Always vs Never). Do not start Phase 3 without that log.
- Strategy detail: `.dev/gprx-design.md` §15.
